        "id": 1940250
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-21T02:20:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At the beginning, here is the macro:hash_for_each in the function, which would check obj if is NULL, so we retain the check.\n\n126  #define hash_for_each(name, bkt, obj, member)\t\t\t\t\\\n127  \tfor ((bkt) \u003d 0, obj \u003d NULL; obj \u003d\u003d NULL \u0026\u0026 (bkt) \u003c HASH_SIZE(name);\\\n128  \t\t\t(bkt)++)\\\n129  \t\thlist_for_each_entry(obj, \u0026name[bkt], member)\n\n\nBut in fact, I think the uid_entry check is unnecessary.\nBecause during for_each_uid_entry-\u003ehlist_for_each_entry, if uid_entry never be NULL, the macro will appear an infinite loop.\n\n1038  #define hlist_for_each_entry(pos, head, member)\t\t\t\t\\\n1039  \tfor (pos \u003d hlist_entry_safe((head)-\u003efirst, typeof(*(pos)), member);\\\n1040  \t     pos;\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\\\n1041  \t     pos \u003d hlist_entry_safe((pos)-\u003emember.next, typeof(*(pos)), member))",
      "parentUuid": "42d4c2fa_9a71e256",
      "revId": "a90b22f101c34868bd4ce73b2dff4a284663c44b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
