      "writtenOn": "2024-03-20T19:21:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems a bit odd.\n\nSo uid_entry is initialized as null, but if uid_entry is somehow left set the last time through the loop, we continue - which will iterate to the next bkt and uid_entry will still remain set, which will iterate to the next bucket, and on...\n\nIt seems like you might as well break there, which is what the original for loop was doing.\n\nI do think it would be cleaner to check `if (uid_entry)` and break after the for_each_uid_entry() loop which sets it, so you don\u0027t have to logically think about the previous iteration.",
      "revId": "a90b22f101c34868bd4ce73b2dff4a284663c44b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
